@startuml consent-flow
!theme cerulean-outline
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam BoxPadding 20
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20

title Cross-bank consent flow

actor "Client App" as App #LightBlue
participant "Bank API" as Bank #ADD8E6
actor "Customer" as Customer #LightYellow

== Simplified prototype scenario ==

note over App, Customer #LightYellow
  This diagram documents a demo consent flow
  used to explain the hackathon prototype idea.
  Identifiers and credentials are placeholders.
end note

App -> Bank: 1. POST /auth/bank-token\nclient_id=demo-team\nclient_secret=***
activate Bank
Bank --> App: 200 OK\n{ access_token: "demo-token" }
deactivate Bank

App -> Bank: 2. POST /account-consents/request\nAuthorization: Bearer {token}\nX-Requesting-Bank: demo-team
activate Bank
Bank --> App: 200 OK\n{ consent_id: "consent-demo", status: "approved" }
deactivate Bank

App -> Bank: 3. GET /accounts\nclient_id=demo-customer\nAuthorization: Bearer {token}\nX-Consent-Id: consent-demo
activate Bank
Bank --> App: 200 OK\n{ accounts: [...] }
deactivate Bank

note over App, Bank #LightGreen
  The public repository keeps this flow as
  an explanatory artifact, not as a full banking product implementation.
end note

@enduml
